<title>USA: Wang settles lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Wang settles lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wang Laboratories Inc has agreed to pay $650,000 in Wang stock to Systemcare Inc to settle a lawsuit, an attorney for Systemcare said on Monday.</p>
<p>Systemcare originally filed a claim for $1.5 million. The settlement follows a decision in late June by the federal appeals court here that reversed itself and re-opened Systemcare's lawsuit against Wang.</p>
<p>Systemcare alleged Wang violated anti-trust law by requiring purchases of its software support services to also purchase its hardware support services.</p>
<p>Systemcare services Wang-built computer hardware. Wang had denied it conditioned the purchase of software suport on the purchase of hardware maintenance, except when a service contract was in effect.</p>
</text>
